I was pretty proud of my self when I got my first tournament ascension. Now
I have two!-) The first one was a lawful elven wizard (third wizard I've
ascended). Two ascensions in four games, I think I play more carefully in
the tournament than I would otherwise. 9th ascension overall.

At the moment this Valkyrie is on the second place in the Valkyrie
category at the tournament.

There was nothing special on the game before I was sacfesting. The first
sacrifice gift was Demonbane, which seemed a bit wierd. Later on I found a
shop a few levels above which had Mjollnir. I never even wielded the
hammer, at the time I was already expert in long sword and had dipped for
Excalibur.

Sokoban yielded "oR and a fruit juice +3 GDSM. The Quest was easy, and with
a tinning kit I maxed my strength. Playing with a polytrap and magic
whistle my cat polyed into a white dragon and when I found a saddle I was
riding around the dungeon with my noble steed.

Castle was also easy and the wand was at (0:1). First wish gave 2
b?oCharging, second bBoH.

VotD had a bonesfile (jore, killed by a vrock) which had the Staff of
Thingy which I couldn't even pick up. I'm not sure, but I might have got
the speed boots from late jore, too.

Rodney double troubled at his tower and /oDeath missed them both twice
before I killed them with the Excalibur and a silver saber I #twoweaponed.

The Sanctum was, well, interesting.. When I had cleared the surrounding
areas, I opened the door to the Sanctum. Two Rodneys were fighting the High
Priestess of Moloch and each other even though I hadn't =oConflict! When I
killed the High Priestess, Moloch sent his pet to see me. Guess what he
sent? No, it wasn't Yeenoghu. It was the Big D.

Fighting two Rodneys, Demogorgon and a horde of summoned monsters was a bit
frightening even though I used Elbereth very liberally. D made me ill
twice and my HP:s went down to (34:287) at the worst. Unicorn horn helped
with the illness, !oFH with the lack of hitpoints.

The elemental planes went fast and the Astral Plane was easiest ever
(because of the low XP?). I started with killing two arch liches, then
headed to face Famine (middle) who was a pushover. Wrong altar, it was
chaotic. This time I didn't want to use [oOA, so Death (right) was next. He
got one hit in, but the altar was the right one. I donated the money in my
main inventory to the High Priest, whistled the Guardian Angel, lit the
Candelabrum and #offered the amulet to Tyr.


